When people die in real life it *seldom* has anything to do with overeating,
it is much more often linked to hurrying, bad eating habits, or a physical 
problem.  I'm unfortunate enough to have seen examples of all three, I've
never seen a glutton choke.  Using your logic characters should choke to
death at random, which would be easy to understand considering their fare.

My point has been that characters should be allowed to "top off" without
fear.  If I go into a gas station and only happen to need 3 gallons I 
don't fear an explosion.  From the outside it would seem like the
"continue eating?" flag could be easily used, if it's not real easy then
I wouldn't ask anyone to waste time but I seem to see a flag that could
be used.  This is a role playing game and can't be real life, but one of
the attractions is seeing it become more complete.

For those who don't understand my concern, towards the end of the game
I often will teleport quite a bit to gather things and put them where 
I will want them later.  Teleporting is safer and saves hours of keyboard 
time, but also uses a lot of energy.  I'd be curious to hear how much an
investment in time a "won" game is for those out there who have done it. 


